Special shopkeepers have a chance to replace regular shopkeepers. Special shopkeepers are unlocked by donating 234 coins to the {{m|Greed Donation Machine}} and special hanging shopkeepers are unlocked by donating 14 coins to the Greed Machine.

=== Possible Rewards ===
* Nothing (~30.09% chance)
* A {{e|Nickel}} / {{e|Sticky Nickel|nr}} (66% chance)
* {{t|Bloody Penny}} / {{t|Butt Penny}} / {{t|Counterfeit Penny}} / {{t|Flat Penny}} / {{t|Swallowed Penny}} / {{t|Burnt Penny}} (3.125% chance)
* {{e|Greed}} (~0.78% chance)
{{clear}}{{dlc clear}}

== Notes ==
* Shopkeepers have 5 hit points, but most attacks capable of hitting them deal more damage than that.
* Non-explosion attacks that can damage shopkeepers include {{i|The Boomerang}}, {{i|Red Candle}}, {{i|The Candle}}, {{i|Stitches}}, and {{i|Mars}}.
** {{dlc|a}} If Isaac has {{i|Holy Light|n}} and hits an enemy near a Shopkeeper with a Holy Light tear, the Shopkeeper will be destroyed by the beam of light.
** {{dlc+|r}} The blast from {{i|Dark Arts}} will hit shopkeepers, but the slicing attack will not. This means an extra target is required to destroy a shopkeeper with Dark Arts. {{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} The blast from {{I|Camo Undies}} will hit shopkeepers. {{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} Collision damage from {{i|Mega Mush}} will hit shopkeepers. {{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} Shopkeepers can be grabbed with {{i|Suplex!}}. The shockwaves may also hit the {{m|Donation Machine}}. {{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r+}} The fire wave generated when colliding with an obstacle using {{i|Mars}} will hit shopkeepers. {{dlc-}}
* Destroying a shopkeeper triggers the effects of specific items and trinkets, such as {{i|Charm of the Vampire}}, {{i|Infestation 2|nr}}, {{t|Samson's Lock|}}, {{i|Lusty Blood|a}}, {{i|Jumper Cables|a+}}, {{i|Book of the Dead|a+}}, {{t|Bat Wing|a+}}, {{i|Athame|r}} and {{t|Sigil of Baphomet|r}}.
** The effects of {{i|Gimpy}}, {{i|Sticky Bombs|a}}, {{i|Infestation 2|r}}, {{i|Vade Retro|r}}, {{i|Vasculitis|r}}, {{i|Quints|r}}, {{i|Hungry Soul|r}} and {{t|Cricket Leg|r}} cannot be triggered by destroying shopkeepers. Destroying shopkeepers also does not provide soul charges for {{i|Urn of Souls|r}}.
* Shopkeepers will be targeted by Mom's foot when using {{p|II - The High Priestess}}.
* Using the <code>PAC1 F1SM</code> [[Seed]] makes Shopkeepers invincible too.
* {{dlc|a}} If {{e|Greed}} appears after destroying a Special Shopkeeper, the doors will be locked.
* {{dlc|a}} If Isaac already has {{i|Steam Sale}}, {{i|Head of the Keeper|n}}, and {{i|Coupon}}, Shopkeepers will not drop any further pedestal items.
* {{dlc|a}} Special Shopkeepers can spawn in some specific room layouts even while not unlocked.

